    "content": "# Plan: Authentication forms\n\nspec: _specs/authentication-forms.md\nbranch: claude/feature/authentication-forms\n\n## Context\nThe spec asks for working email/password forms on `/login` and `/signup`. Each form needs:\n- a show/hide password toggle\n- a submit button labelled \"Log In\" or \"Sign Up\"\n- light validation feedback\n- a link to the other form\n- responsive styling\n\nSubmitting only logs the credentials to the console, because there's no auth yet.\n\nAnswers to the spec's open questions:\n- light email validation\n- no minimum password length\n- no input persistence between the two forms\n- no \"Remember me\" checkbox\n- no \"Forgot password\" link\n\nCurrent state:\n- Both pages are just a title. The login component is wrongly named `SignupPage` and uses `h1`, while signup uses `h2`.\n- `components/AuthForm/` doesn't exist.\n- A leftover untracked `tests/components/AuthForm.test.tsx` from the earlier attempt does exist. Its button labels and behaviour are out of date (it expects the form to clear after submit), and a formatter added semicolons to it.\n\n## Step 0: Branch\nThe spec names `claude/feature/authentication-forms`. We're on `claude/feature/auth-forms`, which has no commits beyond `main`. Create and switch to `claude/feature/authentication-forms`. The untracked spec and test files come along.\n\n## Step 1: `components/AuthForm/` (new)\nFollow the existing component pattern (`components/Avatar/`: component, CSS module, `index.ts` re-export).\n\n**`AuthForm.tsx`**\n- Starts with `\"use client\"`.\n- Props: `{ mode: \"login\" | \"signup\" }`.\n- A per-mode lookup object holds:\n  - the submit label (\"Log In\" / \"Sign Up\")\n  - the switch text and link:\n    - login: \"Don't have an account?\" → \"Sign Up\" `/signup`\n    - signup: \"Already have an account?\" → \"Log In\" `/login`\n  - the password `autoComplete` (`current-password` / `new-password`)\n- State:\n  - `email` and `password` (controlled)\n  - `showPassword` (default `false`)\n  - `errors: { email?: string; password?: string }`\n- Fields:\n  - Each field has a `<label htmlFor>` and an `id`.\n  - Email: `type=\"email\"`, `required`, `autoComplete=\"email\"`.\n  - Password: `type` switches between `password` and `text`, and it's `required`.\n- Toggle: a `type=\"button\"` button with `aria-label` \"Show password\" / \"Hide password\" and `aria-pressed`. It shows `Eye` / `EyeOff` from `lucide-react` and only flips state, so the typed value is kept and rapid toggling is safe.\n- Validation (light): the form uses `noValidate`, so the app shows its own consistent inline messages instead of browser bubbles. The `required` and `type=\"email\"` attributes stay for semantics and autofill.\n  - On submit, `preventDefault()`, then check:\n    - trimmed email is empty → \"Email is required\"\n    - email fails a simple `x@y.z` pattern → \"Enter a valid email address\"\n    - password is empty → \"Password is required\"\n  - If there are errors: set them and don't log anything.\n  - Otherwise: `console.log(\\`${mode} submitted\\`, { email: email.trim(), password })`.\n  - An invalid field gets `aria-invalid=\"true\"` and `aria-describedby` pointing at its error `<p role=\"alert\">` (styled `text-error`).\n  - A field's error clears when the user types in it.\n- No form clearing after submit; the spec doesn't ask for it. Inputs don't persist across pages, because each page mounts its own form.\n- Enter submits the form in the usual way.\n\n**`AuthForm.module.css`**\n- Starts with `@reference \"../../app/globals.css\";`.\n- The form is a column `w-full max-w-sm mx-auto` with gaps between fields.\n- Inputs use `bg-lighter` and `text-heading`, with a `focus-visible` outline in `primary`. Invalid inputs get an `error` outline.\n- The password wrapper is `relative`. The toggle is absolutely positioned on the right, and the input has right padding.\n- The switch link uses `text-primary` and hovers to `text-secondary`.\n- Theme tokens only. The submit button reuses the global `.btn` class (`app/globals.css`).\n\n**`index.ts`**: `export { default } from \"./AuthForm\"`\n\n## Step 2: Pages\n- `app/(public)/login/page.tsx`: rename to `LoginPage`. Change the heading to `h2 className=\"form-title\"` to match signup, which also avoids the larger `.public h1` size. Render `<AuthForm mode=\"login\" />`.\n- `app/(public)/signup/page.tsx`: render `<AuthForm mode=\"signup\" />`.\n- Imports go under `// components`. No semicolons, double quotes.\n\n## Step 3: Responsive fix\nIn `app/globals.css`, `.page-content` uses `min-w-2xl`, which forces horizontal scrolling on phones. That breaks the spec's \"works on mobile\" requirement. Change it to `md:min-w-2xl`, so the minimum width only applies from tablet width up. Desktop layouts on every page stay the same.\n\n## Step 4: Tests\nReplace `tests/components/AuthForm.test.tsx`. Use Testing Library and `@testing-library/user-event`. Spy on `console.log` with `vi.spyOn` and restore it in `afterEach`. Cases:\n- Renders Email, Password and the submit button with the correct label (\"Log In\" / \"Sign Up\") for each mode.\n- Email input has `type=\"email\"` and `required`, and accepts a typed valid address.\n- Password is masked by default and accepts input. The toggle switches it to `text` and back, updating its accessible name.\n- A valid submit logs `\"{mode} submitted\"` with the trimmed email and the password. Also cover submitting with Enter.\n- An empty submit shows \"Email is required\" and \"Password is required\" and doesn't log.\n- An invalid email shows \"Enter a valid email address\" and doesn't log.\n- Login links to `/signup` and signup links to `/login`.\n\n## Verification\n- `npx vitest run`: all suites pass.\n- `npm run lint`: clean.\n- `npm run dev`, then on `/login` and `/signup`:\n  - toggle the password\n  - submit empty, then with a bad email, and check the inline errors\n  - submit valid details and check the console\n  - follow the switch links\n  - try keyboard-only use\n  - try phone width in devtools and check there's no horizontal scroll\n"
